{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he kissed all his brothers and wept upon them.</b> He let them know that there was nothing in his heart against them, and that his mind and will were to do good to them. <b>And after that his brothers spoke with him:</b> for until now speech had been taken from them and they could not speak with him, for they were bewildered before him; and now their minds settled and they spoke with him." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'And he kissed all his brothers' — this teaches that each and every one kissed him and wept, as it says: וינשק לכל אחיו ויבך עליהם. And just as he reconciled his brothers only through weeping, so too does salvation not come to Israel except through weeping, as it says (Jeremiah 31:9): ״בבכי יבאו ובתחנונים אובילם״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:23.381485920Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}